    <!-- Google TV Home button (accessibility service, v0.4.0) -->
    <string name="home_value_google_tv" translatable="false">Google TV</string>
    <string name="a11y_service_label">BSfreeTV Home button</string>
    <string name="a11y_service_desc">Opens BSfreeTV when you press Home. It only listens for the Home button: it cannot see the screen, and it collects and sends nothing. Turn it off to give the Home button back to Google TV.</string>
    <string name="dh_gtv_intro">On Google TV, BSfreeTV can take over the Home button with an accessibility service. Google TV itself stays installed, enabled and untouched.</string>
    <string name="status_override_on">Home button opens BSfreeTV</string>
    <string name="status_override_off">Home button opens Google TV</string>
    <string name="btn_use_home_button">Use Home for BSfreeTV</string>
    <string name="btn_turn_off">Turn off</string>
    <string name="dh_row_hold">Hold Home for Google TV</string>
    <string name="dh_row_hold_on_desc">Press Home for BSfreeTV, hold it for the Google TV home screen</string>
    <string name="dh_row_hold_off_desc">Home always opens BSfreeTV. The only way back to Google TV is turning the service off in Accessibility</string>
    <string name="dh_row_after_restart">Open after restart</string>
    <string name="dh_row_after_restart_desc">Once, right after the TV starts up</string>
    <string name="dh_row_restricted">Switch greyed out?</string>
    <string name="a11y_title">Home button</string>
    <string name="a11y_why">Why an accessibility permission? Google TV does not let you choose another Home app, and switching off its launcher can leave the device restarting in a loop. An accessibility service that catches the Home button is the only safe way to make BSfreeTV your home screen.</string>
    <string name="a11y_does">What it does: it watches for one button, Home. When you press it, BSfreeTV opens. Every other button passes straight through, unchanged.</string>
    <string name="a11y_never">What it never does: it cannot see what is on the screen, does not read what you type or watch, and collects and sends nothing. It does not disable or change Google TV.</string>
    <string name="a11y_warning">Android will warn that the service can observe your actions and control the device. Every accessibility service gets that same warning; BSfreeTV only uses the Home button part.</string>
    <string name="a11y_undo">To undo, switch the service off in Accessibility or uninstall BSfreeTV. The Home button opens Google TV again straight away.</string>
    <string name="a11y_steps">Next: in Accessibility, choose BSfreeTV Home button, turn it on and confirm. Then press Back to return here.</string>
    <string name="btn_open_accessibility">Open Accessibility</string>
    <string name="btn_not_now">Not now</string>
    <string name="restricted_intro">Android may block the switch for apps installed from outside an app store: it shows as greyed out or as a restricted setting. There are two ways to allow it.</string>
    <string name="restricted_app_info">On the TV: open App info for BSfreeTV and choose Allow restricted settings, if your TV shows that option. Then try the switch again.</string>
    <string name="btn_app_info">Open App info</string>
    <string name="restricted_adb">Or let BSfreeTV allow it over Network debugging. This runs a single command that lifts only this block; nothing else on the TV is changed.</string>
    <string name="btn_allow_restricted">Allow with Network debugging</string>
    <string name="task_allow_restricted">Allow restricted settings</string>
